From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: denali-lcd: disable unprotected speakers

The inherited Denali sound card and SoundWire controller enable both
WSA8845 speaker amplifiers. Speaker protection with VI feedback has not
been evidenced on this unit. Disable the card and its speaker bus in the
packaged LCD board DT, as required by project safety rule S1 and D21.

This carries the existing M5/M6 safety overrides into the release DTB.
Keep both disabled until the audio-speakers owner supplies and validates
speaker protection. Kernel owns this temporary integration patch; the
audio-speakers owner is requested to take it over.

Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
@@ -8,6 +8,14 @@
 #include "hamoa.dtsi"
 #include "x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi"
 
+&{/sound} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&swr0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 / {
 	model = "Microsoft Surface Pro 11th Edition (LCD)";
 	compatible = "microsoft,denali-lcd", "microsoft,denali",
